#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git 2.43.1 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:7
msgid ""
"There is nothing exciting to see here.  Relative to Git 2.43, this release "
"contains the fixes that have already been merged to the 'master' branch of "
"the development towards the next major release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since Git 2.43.0"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:13
msgid ""
"The way CI testing used \"prove\" could lead to running the test suite twice "
"needlessly, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:18
msgid ""
"Newer versions of Getopt::Long started giving warnings against our (ab)use "
"of it in \"git send-email\".  Bump the minimum version requirement for Perl "
"to 5.8.1 (from September 2002) to allow simplifying our implementation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:23
msgid ""
"Earlier we stopped relying on commit-graph that (still) records information "
"about commits that are lost from the object store, which has negative "
"performance implications.  The default has been flipped to disable this "
"pessimization."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:26
msgid ""
"Stale URLs have been updated to their current counterparts (or archive.org) "
"and HTTP links are replaced with working HTTPS links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:29
msgid ""
"trace2 streams used to record the URLs that potentially embed authentication "
"material, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:34
msgid ""
"The sample pre-commit hook that tries to catch introduction of new paths "
"that use potentially non-portable characters did not notice an existing path "
"getting renamed to such a problematic path, when rename detection was "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:39
msgid ""
"The command line parser for the \"log\" family of commands was too loose "
"when parsing certain numbers, e.g., silently ignoring the extra 'q' in \"git "
"log -n 1q\" without complaining, which has been tightened up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:43
msgid ""
"\"git $cmd --end-of-options --rev -- --path\" for some $cmd failed to "
"interpret \"--rev\" as a rev, and \"--path\" as a path.  This was fixed for "
"many programs like \"reset\" and \"checkout\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:46
msgid ""
"\"git bisect reset\" has been taught to clean up state files and refs even "
"when BISECT_START file is gone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:49
msgid ""
"Some codepaths did not correctly parse configuration variables specified "
"with valueless \"true\", which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:52
msgid ""
"Code clean-up for sanity checking of command line options for \"git show-"
"ref\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:55
msgid ""
"The code to parse the From e-mail header has been updated to avoid recursion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:58
msgid ""
"\"git fetch --atomic\" issued an unnecessary empty error message, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:61
msgid ""
"Command line completion script (in contrib/) learned to work better with the "
"reftable backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:65
msgid ""
"\"git status\" is taught to show both the branch being bisected and being "
"rebased when both are in effect at the same time.  cf. <xmqqil76kyov."
"fsf@gitster.g>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:68
msgid ""
"\"git archive --list extra garbage\" silently ignored excess command line "
"parameters, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:72
msgid ""
"\"git sparse-checkout set\" added default patterns even when the patterns "
"are being fed from the standard input, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:76
msgid ""
"Unlike other environment variables that took the usual true/false/yes/no as "
"well as 0/1, GIT_FLUSH only understood 0/1, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:81
msgid ""
"Clearing in-core repository (happens during e.g., \"git fetch --recurse-"
"submodules\" with commit graph enabled) made in-core commit object in an "
"inconsistent state by discarding the necessary data from commit-graph too "
"early, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.1.txt:82
msgid ""
"Also contains various documentation updates, code clean-ups and minor fixups."
msgstr ""
